I have what I need. Static review complete; build/test execution was not permitted in this sandbox, so all findings below are source-bound.

{"schema":"uos.agent-review.v1","agent":"claude-code-independent-reviewer","wave":"wave1-t00-t05","verdict":"HOLD","checked_invariants":[{"id":"INV-1-PAYLOAD-ACTOR-NO-ESCALATION","claim":"payload actor/clientInfo cannot escalate Principal","result":"UPHELD_WITHIN_MODULE","evidence":"principal.gleam:8-19 declares `pub opaque type Principal`; the only mutator reachable from payload data, `apply_untrusted_payload_labels` (:78-90), uses a record update that writes solely `untrusted_actor_label`/`untrusted_client_label`/`untrusted_header_actor` and cannot reach `actor_id` or `client_profile`. admission.verify_fenced_mutation binds authority to `principal.actor_id(context.principal)` (admission.gleam:145), never to a label. Law `payload_actor_cannot_change_principal_test` (mcp_admission_test.gleam:11-34) asserts actor_id and client_profile survive a three-vector override attempt.","falsification_attempted":"Searched for any alternate write path to actor_id/client_profile and for any authority decision reading an untrusted_* accessor. Found none.","boundary":"Opacity prevents field mutation, not minting. `from_launcher_env`, `from_http_auth_middleware` and `from_signed_zenoh_envelope` are `pub` and accept an arbitrary actor string with no witness/capability argument, so any module in the package can forge a Stdio Principal for any actor. None of the three verifies the launcher environment, an auth result, or a Zenoh signature — the names assert provenance the code does not check. The invariant therefore rests on call-site discipline, not on the type."},{"id":"INV-2-COMPLETED-TASK-AND-AUDITONLY-CANNOT-AUTHORIZE","claim":"completed Sa-plan tasks and AuditOnly mode cannot authorize mutations","result":"UPHELD","evidence":"admission.gleam:133-143 refuses TaskCompleted with `COMPLETED_TASK_NOT_REUSABLE` and TaskAvailable with `UNCLAIMED_TASK_NOT_AUTHORITATIVE`, both NonRetryable; only TaskExecuting proceeds. AuditOnlyMode x mutation is refused in BOTH `admit` (:74-79) and `verify_at_effect_time` (:88-93), so an AuditOnly context cannot be admitted at t0 nor executed at t1. `is_mutation_effect` (:221-226) enumerates all four EffectClass constructors with no catch-all, so a future effect class breaks the build instead of silently defaulting to non-mutating — correct poka-yoke. Law at mcp_admission_test.gleam:36-102 covers both arms.","falsification_attempted":"Tried to find a mutation path that bypasses the fence: ReadOnly|VerificationGate short-circuits at :105-114, and those classes are excluded from is_mutation_effect, so no mutating spec can reach the unfenced arm. No default/`_ ->` arm exists on spec.effect_class."},{"id":"INV-3-REVOKED-EXPIRED-GRANT-FAILS-CLOSED","claim":"revoked/expired grants fail closed at effect time","result":"UPHELD_CONDITIONALLY","evidence":"verify_grant_ticket (admission.gleam:167-219) refuses None grant (MISSING_AUTHORITY_GRANT), revoked grant (GRANT_REVOKED_AT_EFFECT_TIME when at_effect_time=True), `expires_at_ms <= now_ms` (GRANT_EXPIRED), and workspace mismatch (GRANT_WORKSPACE_MISMATCH), all NonRetryable. Lease uses the same `<=` boundary (:152), so an exactly-expiring lease or grant is refused rather than admitted — correct closed-boundary choice.","falsification_attempted":"Checked whether verify_at_effect_time re-reads authority state. It does not: it re-evaluates the same pure predicates over the `AdmissionContext` the caller hands it. Nothing in admission.gleam reads Sa-plan, the coordinator store, or a clock — `now_ms`, `task_state`, `lease_until_ms` and `grant.revoked` are all caller-asserted.","boundary":"The condition is that the caller constructs a FRESH context from an authoritative source immediately before the effect. `revoked_grant_refused_at_effect_time_test` (:104-164) hand-builds the revoked context, so it proves the predicate, not the refresh. A caller that reuses its t0 context passes effect-time verification with a grant revoked in between, and the code cannot detect it. Time is also caller-supplied, so a context with a stale or attacker-chosen `now_ms` defeats both expiry checks."},{"id":"INV-4-CONFLICTING-PAYLOAD-REUSE-FAILS-CLOSED","claim":"conflicting payload reuse on same intent_id fails closed","result":"UPHELD_FOR_CONFLICT_BUT_COMPLEMENT_FAILS_OPEN","evidence":"receipts.record_intent (receipts.gleam:55-67) returns NonRetryable `IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT` when an existing entry's `payload_hash` or `tool` differs, and worker.run_isolated_with_receipts converts that to `Refused` BEFORE calling `action()` (worker.gleam:35) — pre-dispatch, so the known-no-effect argument holds. hash_payload (:39-46) sorts fields before digesting, so key order cannot forge a hash difference. Law at mcp_worker_recovery_test.gleam:70-100.","falsification_attempted":"Exercised the matching-payload branch. record_intent returns `Ok(ledger)` unchanged; worker.gleam:36-37 then calls `action()` unconditionally, with no inspection of `existing.state`.","defect":"BLOCKING. A replayed intent_id with a MATCHING payload re-executes the mutation instead of returning the recorded `OutcomeCommitted` outcome, so the ledger is not idempotent despite IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT naming. Worse, a replay over an `EffectUncertain` entry also re-runs the effect and then overwrites the uncertain receipt via mark_complete (receipts.gleam:117-134) — erasing the Andon evidence. This contradicts SC-AGENTIC-RESILIENCE-001 Layer 4 (uncertain outcome latches the Andon line until reconciled via harness_reconcile) and SC-LEARN-001 L-09 (a quarantined unknown is not retryable). Minimal fix: in record_intent or at worker entry, branch on existing.state — OutcomeCommitted -> return the stored Outcome without invoking action; EffectUncertain -> Refuse with a reconcile-required code."},{"id":"INV-5-CRITICAL-MODULES-INTACT","claim":"SC-AGENTIC-RESILIENCE-001 critical modules remain intact","result":"UPHELD_BUT_NEW_MODULES_ARE_UNGUARDED","evidence":"harness/admission.gleam:68-80 still declares exactly 28 `control_modules` and `control_dependencies = [\"tools/ecology_process.ml\"]` (:88); the arity law at :432-433 still requires field count == list length. Wave 1 is additive: it introduces mcp/principal, mcp/admission, mcp/receipts, mcp/worker alongside existing mcp/dispatch and mcp/supervisor, and modifies none of the T0-T3 registry paths. mcp/server.gleam imports (:14-27) are unchanged.","falsification_attempted":"Grepped control_modules for any `cepaf_gleam@mcp@*` entry.","gap":"No MCP-route module — not the new authority modules, and not even the contract's own T2 entries `cepaf_gleam@mcp@server`/`tools`/`protocol`/`authz` — appears in control_modules. The Layer-3 BEAM-MD5 guard therefore does not cover the modules that now decide MCP authority: they can be recompiled or hot-loaded without producing `loaded_control_digest_mismatch`. The T2 row of the contract already overstates the live registry; Wave 1 widens the uncovered surface."},{"id":"INV-6-RUNTIME-WIRING","claim":"not asserted by the plan; verified independently","result":"NOT_WIRED","evidence":"`grep -c` for mcp/admission|mcp/principal|mcp/dispatch|mcp/worker|mcp/receipts in mcp/server.gleam returns 0. server.gleam:1058-1086, 1104-1132 and 1150-1183 still decode `params.arguments.worker` from the request payload and pass it directly to sa_plan_bridge.claim_sa_task / complete_sa_task / enqueue_sa_job with no Principal, no fence and no grant.","consequence":"The payload-actor escalation that Principal exists to prevent is STILL LIVE on the public server path. Wave 1 is a parallel, currently inert pipeline. This is acceptable for a foundation wave only if no runtime-enforcement claim is attached to it; it is not a basis for closing any authority checklist item."}],"advice_for_t06_t24":["T06 FIRST, before any further surface: fix the receipts replay semantics. Make record_intent (or worker entry) return the stored Outcome for OutcomeCommitted and refuse EffectUncertain with a reconcile-required NonRetryable code. Add three laws: matching replay must NOT invoke the action closure (assert via a counter in the closure), uncertain replay must refuse, and reconcile must be the only transition out of EffectUncertain.","Make the authority context unforgeable rather than asserted. Replace the three bare Principal constructors with ones that consume a provenance witness only the launcher/HTTP middleware/Zenoh verifier can produce (e.g. an opaque LauncherEnv read inside principal.gleam, an opaque AuthnResult, a verified-signature token). Until then, document in the module header that minting is call-site-trusted — the current header claims more than the code enforces.","Make effect-time verification actually re-read authority. verify_at_effect_time should take a reader (fn() -> Result(TaskFence, ToolError)) plus a monotonic clock source rather than a caller-supplied AdmissionContext, so a grant revoked between t0 and t1 is observed. Add a law where the fence reader flips revoked between admit and effect time with the SAME context value passed in, and the call must still refuse — today that test cannot be written.","Bind workspace in all four directions. admission compares grant.workspace_root to context.workspace_root but never to principal.workspace_root, and the ReadOnly/VerificationGate arm (admission.gleam:105-114) checks workspace not at all. Add principal.workspace_root == context.workspace_root as a precondition for every effect class, with a law for a cross-workspace principal (relevant under SC-WORKSPACE-ISO-001 INV-WS-05).","Register the MCP authority modules in harness/admission control_modules, or state explicitly in the contract that MCP-route modules are outside the Layer-3 MD5 guard. Do not leave the contract's T2 row asserting coverage the list does not provide. Adding entries changes the 28-count and the grant manifest, so this needs its own reviewed grant — plan it as a discrete task, not a side effect.","Make the ledger durable or rename it. receipts.gleam is headed \"Durable Receipt Ledger\" but is an in-memory Dict with no persistence; a worker crash loses exactly the records crash-reconciliation depends on. Either back it with the append-only SQLite store (Psi-1 regenerative completeness) or correct the header and the plan language to \"in-process\".","Tighten the replay identity key. record_intent compares only tool and payload_hash; route, actor/principal, plan/task/attempt and ledger candidate are stored but never compared. Two different actors, routes or candidates sharing an intent_id are treated as the same intent. dispatch_validated derives intent_id from route+name+hash so it is safe there, but execute_on_pool and any external caller pass arbitrary ids.","Remove the fabricated default in mark_uncertain (receipts.gleam:93-96): an unknown intent_id yields route \"public\", tool \"unknown\" and a receipt that names a route it never used. Return a Result instead — an uncertain receipt for an unrecorded intent is itself an integrity defect.","Delete or quarantine the SimulatedCrash* constructors from the production path before wiring. WorkerActionResult (worker.gleam:10-16) exposes SimulatedCrashBeforeEffect/AfterEffect in the same public type the real dispatcher consumes; a caller can mint an Uncertain receipt and latch Andon with no real effect. Move simulation behind a test-only module or a mode flag that EnforcedMode rejects.","When wiring server.gleam (the step that makes any of this real), treat it as a T2 critical-code change: task-scoped grant, CAS expected-sha256, and the 184-test gate. Replace the three payload-`worker` decoders at :1058/:1104/:1150 with principal-derived worker identity in the same change that introduces the fence — leaving both paths live would give an attacker the choice of door.","Keep the claim ladder honest in the T06-T24 journals: these modules are specification + unit laws. They are not a runtime observation and not admission. EV ceiling stays 93; no new EV number."],"residual_risks":[{"id":"RR-01","severity":"high","risk":"Uncertain-effect replay re-executes the mutation and overwrites the uncertain receipt, so a crash-after-effect followed by a retry can double-apply an effect and destroy the Andon evidence that would have revealed it.","detectability":"low — no law currently exercises matching-payload replay, so the suite is green while the defect is present."},{"id":"RR-02","severity":"high","risk":"admission.gleam is a pure validator over caller-asserted facts. It never reads Sa-plan, the coordinator store, or a clock. A caller that fabricates TaskExecuting + a fresh unrevoked grant + a favourable now_ms is admitted. All five invariants are conditional on the integrity of whatever builds AdmissionContext, which Wave 1 does not supply."},{"id":"RR-03","severity":"high","risk":"Live payload-actor escalation persists in mcp/server.gleam (params.arguments.worker -> sa_plan_bridge). Wave 1 changes nothing observable on the public MCP surface; a reader of the plan could mistake module existence for enforcement."},{"id":"RR-04","severity":"medium","risk":"Principal provenance is nominal. Three public constructors mint any actor_id with the transport label of their choice and verify nothing; a mis-wired or malicious in-package call site produces an authoritative-looking Stdio principal."},{"id":"RR-05","severity":"medium","risk":"The new MCP authority modules sit outside the 28-module BEAM-MD5 guard, so hot-code drift in the authority decision path raises no loaded_control_digest_mismatch."},{"id":"RR-06","severity":"medium","risk":"Receipt ledger is non-durable in-memory state; crash loses the reconciliation record the design depends on (Psi-1)."},{"id":"RR-07","severity":"medium","risk":"Simulation constructors are reachable from the production WorkerActionResult type, allowing synthetic Uncertain outcomes and Andon latching without any real effect."},{"id":"RR-08","severity":"low","risk":"Workspace root is unchecked on read-only calls and never cross-checked against the principal's own workspace, weakening SC-WORKSPACE-ISO-001 isolation for MCP reads."},{"id":"RR-09","severity":"low","risk":"Contract-to-code drift pre-existing Wave 1: SC-AGENTIC-RESILIENCE-001 T2 names four cepaf_gleam@mcp@* modules as MD5-guarded critical code, but control_modules contains no mcp entry. Recorded, not repaired here."},{"id":"RR-10","severity":"low","risk":"This review is source-bound only. Build and EUnit execution were refused by the sandbox, so the 184/184 gate and the three Wave 1 laws are UNRUN in this review; green-test status is reported by others, not observed by me."}]}
